  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Paredes + Alemán Arquitectos, Zona 10, Guatemala City; the medical tower was begun by Davide Garda): at the street corner the food-court building is a faceted two-storey volume, turned to face the corner, clad in grey-cream panels with a tall glazed window wall set in an angled frame (a steel box edge above and below), over a ground floor of slim steel columns and a dark glass base; behind it a lobby with a matrix of pyramidal skylights, honey-timber benches and planters, tall angled stone fins with gilt edges, a vertical white louvre wall; behind that a blue-glass medical tower with banded floors (the glass tower is visible beside the food court in the first photograph). Modelled: the tower (30 m of glass and slab bands, a smaller step at the top), the lobby block with its skylights, the angled food-court volume on columns with its corner window wall, street, planting. Guessed: the tower's height and plan (a glimpse in one photograph), the lobby's length, the plot's depth and the street layout (the article puts it at the corner of 6th and 7th Avenues, Zone 10). A public commercial and clinic building, placed at its own spot (OpenStreetMap building way 400891967)."
